---
const rows = [
  ["Reason", "because, since, as", "We stayed inside because it was raining."],
  ["Time", "when, while, before, after, until, whenever", "When the bell rang, the children left."],
  ["Condition", "if, unless", "If it rains, we will stay inside."],
  ["Contrast", "although, though, even though", "Although it was cold, we went outside."],
  ["Purpose", "so that", "We left early so that we would be on time."]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Conjunctions</h1>
  <p class="topic-lead">Subordinating conjunctions</p>
  <p>
    A subordinating conjunction introduces a subordinate clause and shows how that idea relates to the main
    idea. Group them by meaning, not as one long list.
  </p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-mint">
    <h2>Useful groups</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Relationship</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Conjunctions</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Example</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          rows.map(([kind, words, example]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{kind}</th>
              <td>{words}</td>
              <td>{example}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  <div class="summary-stack">
    <section class="summary-block summary-yellow">
      <h2>Unless means if…not</h2>
      <p>We will go outside <strong>unless</strong> it rains.</p>
      <p>We will go outside <strong>if it does not rain</strong>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="summary-block summary-peach">
      <h2>The subordinate clause can move</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>When the bell rang,</strong> the children left. Clause first: use a comma.
      </p>
      <p>
        The children left <strong>when the bell rang</strong>. Clause second: usually no comma.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same comma pattern works for <em>because</em>, <em>although</em> and <em>if</em>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="summary-block summary-lilac">
      <h2>Not the same as who, which or that</h2>
      <p>
        The girl <strong>who won the race</strong> received a medal. <em>Who</em> starts a relative clause.
      </p>
      <p>
        The girl ran home <strong>because she was tired</strong>. <em>Because</em> gives the reason.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
